      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "The Camera Behaves Like the Browser",
        "statement": "Zooming the browser should zoom the Twilite camera, and the mouse wheel should act on the surface under the pointer the way it would on any web page: scroll it if it can scroll, and when nothing there can, the wheel belongs to the camera, which zooms about the middle of the screen. A person should never see a scrollbar that does nothing, and should never have to learn a second set of zoom and scroll rules for Twilite.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "unproven",
        "notes": "Raised from a real failure: a page view hosted in a workspace graph showed a scrollbar that the wheel could not scroll. Michael decided two things along the way: zooming about the centre of the screen is the most humane choice, so zoom stays centred and is not moved under the pointer; and the plain wheel over the workspace zooming the camera is fine, which makes Ctrl+wheel nothing special. The code that decides who owns a wheel event already exists (components/NodeGraph/interactionArbiter.js in the twilite repo).",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "zoom-and-wheel-behavior"
        },
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Lightbulb"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea.node-class.node"
      },
