      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        },
        {
          "id": "surface-delegate",
          "key": "surface-delegate",
          "portId": "surface-delegate",
          "label": "surface delegate",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 90,
          "role": "view.content"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Camera Behaves Like the Browser\n\nZoom in the browser zooms the camera, and the wheel acts on the surface under the pointer the way it does on the web: it scrolls that surface if it can, and when nothing there can scroll, the camera takes the wheel and zooms about the middle of the screen.\n\n**Built:** Ctrl+wheel, pinch and the Ctrl plus, minus and zero keys drive the camera. A page view at workspace level scrolls. A card with nothing to scroll no longer swallows the wheel. A test bench checks each case.\n\n**The contract is now one ordered list** in wheelContract.js, asked by the canvas, the frames and the nodes, and tested as data.\n\n**Still open:** latching a gesture to its surface, menu zoom, and frames the page cannot read."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true,
          "surfaceDelegation": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "zoom-and-wheel-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
